text.section:
No retail establishment shall sell or offer for retail sale for outdoor use a plant that is an invasive plant species unless such retail establishment posts in a conspicuous manner on the property located in proximity to each invasive plant display signage identifying such plant as invasive, educating consumers regarding invasive plant species, and encouraging consumers to ask about alternatives. For purposes of this subsection, "invasive plant species" means the following list of plants:

Acer platanoides;


Akebia quinata;


Albizia julibrissin;


Arum italicum;


Berberis thunbergii;


Buddleja davidii;


Cenchrus purpurascens;


Citrus trifoliata;


Clematis terniflora;


Egeria densa;


Elaeagnus pungens;


Euonymus alatus;


Euonymus fortunei;


Glechoma hederacea;


Hedera helix;


Iris pseudacorus;


Ligustrum sinense;


Lonicera fragrantissima;


Lysimachia nummularia;


Mahonia bealei;


Miscanthus sinensis;


Morus alba;


Murdannia keisak;


Myriophyllum aquaticum;


Nandina domestica;


Oshuna crassipes;


Paulownia tomentosa;


Perilla frutescens;


Phyllostachys aurea;


Pyrus calleryana;


Rubus phoenicolasius;


Securigera varia;


Spiraea japonica;


Triadica sebifera;


Tripidium ravennae;


Vinca major;


Vinca minor;


Wisteria floribunda; and


Wisteria sinensis.
